{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9116-1",
  "summary": "netkit-rsh vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that the rcp client in rsh incorrectly handled filenames\nof . or empty filenames received from the server. If a user were tricked\ninto connecting to a malicious rsh server, an attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to modify the permissions of the target directory.\n(CVE-2019-7282)\n\nIt was discovered that the rcp client in rsh did not properly validate\nfilenames received from the server. If a user were tricked into connecting\nto a malicious rsh server, an attacker could possibly use this issue to\noverwrite arbitrary files in the target directory. (CVE-2019-7283)",
